    'Whole-body integration: this transition shares direct technical overlap with a controlled push-up negative — someone who has trained push-up eccentric control elsewhere has a real head start on doing this transition safely.',
    'Common mistake: letting the hips sag or the shoulders dive below elbow height during the lowering phase, which places significant, often cumulative strain on the shoulder joint — this is one of the more common sources of shoulder irritation in a regular yoga practice.',
