    'Execution: hinge forward from the hips (the same hip-hinge principle as Triangle Pose), leading with the chest rather than the head, reaching only as far as the hips allow before the lower back begins to round.',
    'Whole-body integration: this is functionally the seated, symmetrical version of the same hip-hinge and hamstring-length principles covered in Triangle Pose and the Strength Fundamentals hinge group — the joint mechanics are identical, only the position changes.',
    'Common mistake: rounding the entire spine to get the head or chest closer to the legs, which shifts the stretch away from the hamstrings and onto the lower back — a bent-knee version with a straight spine trains the intended target far better than a straight-leg version with a rounded back.',
